    "overview": "By month eleven you've had a deal go sideways, a month with no closings, or both. That's not a sign you picked the wrong career — it's the part of the job nobody puts in the recruiting brochure. This month is about the two skills that separate agents who last from agents who quit: solving problems calmly under contract, and staying in motion when the results aren't showing up yet.",
